## Claude Code authoring best practices (2026)

Distilled from <https://code.claude.com/docs>: current as of
ai-config-kit 0.3.0. Cited inline so you can verify each rule
at the source.

### Size + structure

- **Target under 200 lines per CLAUDE.md.** Longer files consume
  more context and reduce adherence. Split large content into
  [`.claude/rules/`](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory#organize-rules-with-claude/rules/)
  with `paths:` frontmatter so rules only load when matching files
  are touched.
- **Use markdown headers and bullets**, not dense paragraphs.
  Cited: <https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory#write-effective-instructions>.
- **Specificity wins**: "Use 2-space indentation" beats "Format code
  properly". Concrete instructions are verifiable.

### File hierarchy (load order, root → leaf)

1. **Managed policy** (`/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/CLAUDE.md`
   on macOS, `/etc/claude-code/CLAUDE.md` on Linux/WSL,
   `C:\Program Files\ClaudeCode\CLAUDE.md` on Windows): IT-controlled.
2. **User** (`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`): personal preferences, all projects.
3. **Project** (`./CLAUDE.md` or `./.claude/CLAUDE.md`): committed,
   team-shared.
4. **Local** (`./CLAUDE.local.md`): gitignored, personal-per-project.
5. **Nested CLAUDE.md** in subdirectories: load on-demand when
   Claude reads files there.

All files **concatenate, root-down**. Later files can't override
earlier ones: they accumulate. Avoid conflicts; remove duplicates.

### Imports

`@path/to/file` inline-expands another file at session start. Max
depth 5. Relative paths resolve to the file containing the import.
Cited: <https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory#import-additional-files>.

For shared instructions across worktrees of the same repo:

```text
# Individual Preferences
- @~/.claude/my-project-instructions.md
```

### AGENTS.md compat

Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md`, **not** `AGENTS.md`. Bridge the two:

```markdown
@AGENTS.md

## Claude-specific
- (your additions here)
```

Or symlink: `ln -s AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md` (on Windows needs Admin /
Developer Mode).

### Skills (replaces custom slash commands)

As of Claude Code v2.x, `.claude/commands/` files are still honoured,
but `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` is the modern equivalent and
adds:

- A directory for supporting files (templates, scripts, examples).
- Frontmatter for invocation control (`disable-model-invocation`,
  `user-invocable`, `context: fork`, `allowed-tools`, `paths`).
- Auto-loading when relevant to the user's prompt.

Cited: <https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills>.

**When to use a skill** vs CLAUDE.md content:

- *Reference content* (style guides, conventions) → CLAUDE.md (always loaded).
- *Multi-step procedures* (deploy, commit, fix-issue) → skill (loads on demand).
- *Knowledge that's only relevant in some files* → `.claude/rules/` with `paths:`.

**Use `disable-model-invocation: true`** on skills with side
effects: `/deploy`, `/commit`, `/send-slack-message`. Stops Claude
from "helpfully" running them.

**Use `context: fork`** on read-heavy skills (research, audits)
so they run in a forked subagent and don't pollute the main
context window. Pair with an `agent: Explore` / `agent: Plan`
designation.

### Hooks vs CLAUDE.md

**CLAUDE.md is context**, delivered as a user message after the
system prompt. Claude reads it and tries to follow it; there's no
strict enforcement.

**Hooks are enforced**: they run as shell commands at lifecycle
events regardless of what Claude decides to do. Use hooks for
must-run actions like "lint before every commit" or "block PUT
requests to production".

34 hook events as of 2026; full list at
<https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks>. Notable:

- `PreToolUse`: block / deny / ask / defer tool calls.
- `UserPromptSubmit`: pre-process or block user input.
- `PostToolUse`: observability only.
- `SessionStart`: inject startup context.
- `PreCompact` / `PostCompact`: last-chance state save before context summary.
- `InstructionsLoaded`: debug which CLAUDE.md / rules files loaded.

### Auto memory

Claude Code maintains per-project notes at
`~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/MEMORY.md`. The first 200 lines /
25KB are loaded at every session start.

- **Audit + edit** via `/memory` from a session.
- **Disable** via `autoMemoryEnabled: false` in settings or
  `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY=1`.

### Anti-patterns to avoid

- **No secrets in CLAUDE.md.** It goes to the model on every session.
- **No conversation paste** (`User said X, I replied Y…`): move to
  auto memory or skill body.
- **No multi-step procedure dumps**: extract to a skill.
- **No "always do X **and** never do Y" pairs that are easy to
  conflict**: pick the positive form, drop the negative.
- **No outdated references**: `commands/` → use `skills/` for new
  work; `AGENTS.md` not directly read: must be imported.

### `/init` bootstrap

Run `claude /init` in a fresh repo to generate a starting CLAUDE.md.
It analyses the codebase + reads any `AGENTS.md` / `.cursorrules` /
`.windsurfrules` and merges relevant parts.

Set `CLAUDE_CODE_NEW_INIT=1` for the interactive multi-phase flow
that proposes skills + hooks alongside CLAUDE.md.

### HTML-comment trick

`<!-- maintainer note: rotate this token quarterly -->` style
comments in CLAUDE.md are **stripped before** the content reaches
the model. Free space for human-only notes.

Cited: <https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory#how-claude-md-files-load>.

### When `/compact` happens

Project-root CLAUDE.md survives compaction: re-read from disk after
the summary. Nested CLAUDE.md files in subdirectories do NOT
re-inject; they reload the next time Claude reads a file there.

If you have a critical rule and `/compact` keeps dropping it, hoist
it to the project-root CLAUDE.md.
